# Continuous-branch Y-fork demo for paper figure (连续分支分叉演示)
# 
# Geometry: thick trunk → fork → continuing child B nearly collinear with parent
# (slight bend), side child C thinner at moderate angle ~55°.
# Radii: parent ≈ continuing child; side branch clearly thinner but not extreme.
#
# This SWC demonstrates the convex-hull junction flaw in the continuous-branch
# case: the hull wraps bulkily around the smooth continuation, swallowing the
# gentle crotch and losing the continuous-tube appearance, while the Y-Fork
# method preserves the main continuation as a bent pipe with a clean side port.
#
